'''Attributes''' are special passive abilities and buffs typically obtained through {{Skill|Hunting}}. Each Attribute has a corresponding '''Attribute Shard''', a type of item that is automatically stored in the player's [[#Hunting Box|Hunting Box]] when obtained. These can also be [[#Attribute Fusion|fused]] into other shards, or syphoned into their respective attribute, with more syphons increasing the attribute's level, up to level {{Green|10}}.

== Obtaining ==
'''Attribute Shards''' are obtained in multiple ways:
* {{Skill|Hunting}} mobs with [[Critter Capsule]]s, [[Fishing Net]]s, [[Lasso]]s, or [[Black Hole]]s.
* Killing mobs that have a shard with {{Stat|charm chance}}.
* Dropping from certain {{mcat|bosses}}, {{mcat|slayer bosses}}, {{mcat|minibosses}}, {{mcat|slayer minibosses}}
* Using [[Huntraps]] in certain locations.
* Fusing with the [[Fusion Machine]].
* Reward from [[Tree Gifts]].
* Rewards chests in [[Kuudra]] and [[Dungeons]].
* Purchased from {{NPCSprite|Agatha}}, {{NPCSprite|Miria}}, {{NPCSprite|Kiara}} and {{NPCSprite|Sanger}}.
* Crafting Recipes

Attributes can be turned on or off in the Attribute menu.

=== Attribute Fusion ===
{{Main|Attribute Fusion}}
{{Green|5}} '''Attributes''' can be fused to create new '''Attributes'''. '''Reptilian''', '''Elemental''', and '''Amphibian Attributes''' only require {{Green|2}} to fuse. The resulting fusions can be previewed before confirming. Both sets of '''Attributes''' are consumed in the process.

== Requirements ==
Most '''Attributes''' require the following {{Skill|Hunting}} levels to Syphon:
*{{Common}} – 0
*{{Uncommon}} – 5
*{{Rare}} – 10
*{{Epic}} – 15
*{{Legendary}} – 20

Attributes that existed prior to {{Skill|Hunting}} have no requirement, except for {{Attr|Attack Speed}} ({{Item|Inferno Demonlord Shard}}), which has the standard {{Skill|Hunting|15}} requirement.

== Hunting Box ==
The '''Hunting Box''' is a menu that stores Attribute Shards. It can be accessed from the {{Skill|Hunting}} Skill menu or from the <code>/huntingbox</code> command. Any Attribute Shards that are collected automatically get sent to the '''Hunting Box'''. 

While in the Hunting Box, Attribute Shards can be syphoned into an attribute, or [[Attribute Fusion|Fused]] into a new attribute. The box can be sorted by ID and newest. Shards can also be right-clicked to be taken out from the box and turned into an item.

Clicking the chest at the top of the menu allows the player to swap from the '''Hunting Box''' to the Attribute Menu.
{{:Hunting Box/UI}}

== Leveling ==
'''Attribute Shards''' can be syphoned to the [[#Hunting Box|Hunting Box]] by pressing {{keypress|Right-Click}} while holding them. Pressing {{keypress|Left-Click}} an '''Attribute''' in the [[#Hunting Box|Hunting Box]] syphons it and contributes towards leveling up its respective '''Attribute'''.

'''Attributes''' begin at Level {{green|{{romnum|1}}}} ({{Green|1}}) and can be upgraded up to Level {{green|{{romnum|10}}}} ({{Green|10}}) by syphoning more shards. Higher [[Rarity]] Attributes require less shards to increase their levels. The amount of '''Attribute Shards''' required to reach max level for each rarity of an '''Attribute''' is as follows:

