== Tips ==
* Regarding {{Item|Silentdepth Shard}} and {{Item|Thyst Shard}}:
**Because their hunting methods overlap in the {{Zone|Jungle}}, it is recommended to place [[Huntraps|{{red|Huntraps}}]] in one of the other 3 quadrants.
**Reliable bodies of water can be found : 
*** in the {{Zone|Lost Precursor City}} 
*** in the {{Zone|Goblin Holdout}} at {{Coords|361|166|526}}.
**Alternatively, one can use {{Item|Wooden Bait}} in the {{Zone|Crystal Hollows}} to guarantee reeling in {{Item|Silentdepth Shard}}(s) as their next {{Catch|Good}}.

== Bugs ==
* {{Item|Thyst Shard}}’s hunting area remains extended across all 4 quadrants despite its description. Thus, {{Item|Silentdepth Shard}} cannot be hunted specifically from [[Huntraps]]. 
**A secure alternative is to use {{Item|Wooden Bait}}s.
*{{Item|Wisp Pet}}s are affected by the {{Attr|Battle Experience}} attribute when being fed [[Gabagool]]s, despite it not being from Combat.

== Trivia ==
* Prior to 0.23, '''Attributes''' were bound to items. Items could be fused together at {{NPCSprite|Igor}} or {{NPCSprite|Alwin}} to increase their level.
* '''Attribute Shards''' generally follow the {{Dark Green|Forest}}, {{Aqua|Water}}, {{Red|Combat}} pattern when ordered by ID. Gaps in IDs likely exist as a reservation for future shards of the corresponding category.
**{{Item|Fenlord Shard}} (E7) used to be {{Aqua|Water}} instead of the expected {{Dark Green|Forest}}, but this was changed.
**{{Item|Starborn Shard}} (L44) used to be {{Red|Combat}} instead of the expected {{Aqua|Water}}, but this was changed.
* {{item|Bezal Shard}} ({{Attr|Blazing Resistance}})'s head icon is an upside-down version of the {{item|Plushie Blaze Skin}}.
* {{item|Naga Shard}} ({{Attr|Charmed}}) head icon is Duke Fishron from Terraria.
* {{Attr|Lifeline}} ({{item|Kada Knight Shard}}) may be based off a ''League of Legends'' passive of the same name, with similar activation requirements and effects.
* {{Attr|Unlimited Power}} ({{item|Jormung Shard}}) may be a reference to ''Star Wars'', specifically a quote in ''Revenge of the Sith'' by Darth Sidious.
* {{Attr|Vitality}} ({{item|Kraken Shard}}) internal name is {{code|mending}} as it used to be called that way.
* Prior to '''0.24.5''', the {{Item|Hellwisp Shard}} and the {{Item|Inferno Demonlord Shard}} (then known as {{Item|Burningsoul Shard}}) had each other's IDs and rarities. When the update dropped, all previous instances of either shards syphoned were swapped, but unsyphoned shards were unchanged. A player who had Level 10 {{Attr|Matriarch Cubs}} '''Attribute''' prior to the update will instead have Level 10 {{Attr|Attack Speed}} '''Attribute''' instead.
** This change was made to ensure players did not need to re-hunt Attributes they had already maxed out. However, '''0.27''' changed the {{Item|Thorn Shard}} and {{Item|Scarf Shard}} from {{Rarity|Legendary}} to {{Rarity|Epic}}, breaking this consistency.
* Changelog from '''0.24.5''' is mistaken as {{Attribute|Crystal Serendipity}} ({{item|Silentdepth Shard}}) has been functional on lock-pickable chests since '''0.24.1'''.
* As of '''0.27,''' {{Item|Bitbug Shard}} cannot be fused into via {{Item|Chameleon Shard}}, and {{Item|Grizzly Bear Shard}} cannot be fused with {{Item|Chameleon Shard}}.
** This is likely to prevent progression skipping, as otherwise one would be able to easily acquire {{Item|Molthorn Shard}} for extremely cheap.
*The {{Item|Rainbug Shard}} is the only shard that has its method of unlocking obfuscated in the menu.

